# ews2-bypass.wv
# E36 M52 EWS2 Chassis Bypass + Starter / Alternator Supplemental Wiring — Phase 1
#
# !! CHASSIS MODIFICATION — NOT A HARNESS BUILD !!
# This file documents the OEM chassis wiring changes required when replacing the
# OEM MS41 DME with MaxxECU. MaxxECU has no EWS rolling-code communication,
# so the EWS2 immobilizer must be bypassed. Without bypass: cranks, will not fire.
#
# Source: https://falkmfg.com/blogs/news/how-to-bypass-ews2-for-e36-bmw
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BACKGROUND — EWS2 System
#
#   EWS2 (Electronic Vehicle Immobilizer 2) is fitted to OBD2 E36 M52 cars
#   (1995–1998 US spec). The EWS2 module sits behind the glovebox and reads
#   the key transponder via the ignition lock ring antenna.
#
#   Starter inhibit path:
#     Kl.15 IGN (+12V) → EWS2 module pin 1
#     If key transponder valid: EWS2 passes signal to pin 3 → starter relay coil
#     If key transponder invalid: pin 3 is open → starter relay never energizes → no crank
#
#   IMMO signal path:
#     EWS2 module pin 4 → serial K-line rolling code to OEM MS41 DME
#     If code matches: DME enables fuel/spark
#     With MaxxECU replacing the DME: this wire goes nowhere useful;
#     MaxxECU ignores it entirely.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EWS2 MODULE LOCATION
#
#   Behind the glovebox — the glovebox drops on the lower hinge to expose the
#   EWS2 module mounted to the structural cross-member. 4-pin Bosch connector
#   (gray housing) + ring antenna lead (2-wire, to ignition lock ring).
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EWS2 CONNECTOR PINOUT (4-pin, gray housing, behind glovebox)
#
#   Pin 1 — Kl.15 IGN ON  : +12V from ignition switch (key positions II, III)
#   Pin 2 — GND            : Chassis ground
#   Pin 3 — Starter enable : Output to starter relay coil (EWS-controlled)
#   Pin 4 — IMMO K-line    : Serial rolling-code line to OEM DME MS41 pin
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BYPASS PROCEDURE — HARD-WIRE METHOD
#
# Step 1 — Bridge pins 1 and 3 at the EWS2 connector
#   Cut or pull pin 4 from the EWS2 connector. Install a short jumper wire
#   (18 AWG minimum) bridging pin 1 (IGN+) and pin 3 (starter relay coil).
#   Effect: starter relay coil now gets +12V directly whenever the key is in
#   the START position, bypassing EWS gate.
#
#   WARNING: The OEM park/neutral switch (auto transmission inhibit relay) is
#   not affected by this bypass. However, with MaxxECU 8HP GEN1 control, the
#   8HP TCU reports range position (P/R/N/D) to MaxxECU via CAN. MTune can
#   implement a software starter inhibit using the 8HP range position — no
#   additional hardware relay is needed. Configure MTune :: 8HP :: Starter
#   inhibit to allow crank only in P or N before first start.
#
# Step 2 — Isolate pin 4 (IMMO K-line)
#   Remove pin 4 from the EWS2 connector body or cut and tape the wire back.
#   This line connected to the OEM DME MS41 — with MaxxECU replacing the DME,
#   the wire stub goes nowhere. Isolating it prevents any residual EWS2 signal
#   from floating. The EWS2 module will log a "key mismatch" fault code but
#   this does not cause a CEL and has no effect on MaxxECU operation.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ALTERNATOR D+ EXCITE WIRE — M50 Harness 12-pin Extra Pin 12 (M)
#
# Source: maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-terminated_engine_harness-bmw_m50.html
#         Installation step 8
#
#   The M52 alternator is internally-regulated (Bosch IR/EL-type). The D+
#   terminal (alternator excitation input) requires a small current path to
#   +12V IGN to initiate charging. Without this wire, the alternator will not
#   regulate output below ~1,500–2,000 RPM and the battery will not charge.
#
#   Wiring: IGN +12V (switched, relay-protected) → charge bulb (3–5W dashboard
#   bulb, e.g., W5W bayonet) → 12-pin extra connector pin 12 (M) → alternator D+
#
#   The charge bulb illuminates as a "battery" warning light when the alternator
#   is not charging; extinguishes once alternator output voltage exceeds IGN supply.
#   This is the standard "battery warning" indicator behavior — wire through the
#   OEM instrument cluster battery warning bulb if desired, or use a standalone
#   bulb in the engine bay.
#
#   Wire: 18 AWG, yellow/black or yellow (OEM charge lamp color convention)
#   Fuse: 5A inline, source side of the bulb
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STARTER TRIGGER SIGNAL — M50 Harness 12-pin Extra Pin 6 (F)
#
# Source: maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-terminated_engine_harness-bmw_m50.html
#         Installation step 9; 12-pin connector REV2 pinout, pin 6 (F)
#
#   Pin 6 (F) is the ENGINE STARTER TRIGGER input to MaxxECU. This is NOT the
#   high-current starter motor wire — it is a signal wire that tells MaxxECU
#   when the key is in the START position. MaxxECU uses this for cranking
#   enrichment, anti-stall during start, and starter inhibit logic.
#
#   Wiring: Ignition switch START position (+12V, key position III only) →
#           12-pin extra connector pin 6 (F)
#
#   The high-current starter motor circuit is unchanged from OEM E36 wiring
#   (battery → fuse → starter solenoid main terminal; starter relay contact
#   → starter solenoid control). Only the EWS2 coil-side bypass (steps 1–2
#   above) modifies the starter relay control circuit.
#
#   Wire: 18 AWG, red/yellow (OEM start signal color convention)
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PHASE 1 WIRING CHECKLIST — M52 + MaxxECU M50 Harness SUPPLEMENTAL
#
# Items COVERED by the M50 pre-terminated harness (do not build):
#   - Injectors 1–6 (JPT/EV1 connectors)
#   - Coil-on-plug ignition 1–6 (VAG 4-way COP connectors)
#   - Crank sensor (60-2 VR, BMW connector)
#   - Cam/HOME sensor (requires swap to BMW 12141726590 for VANOS head)
#   - IAT sensor
#   - CLT sensor
#   - TPS (OEM M52 throttle body)
#   - MAP sensor (hose included in harness)
#   - Wideband O2 — LSU 4.2 (Bosch 6-pin connector)
#   - VANOS solenoid — GPO 3 (JPT 2-way connector)
#   - ICV idle control valve — GPO 4 + GPO 5 (JPT 3-way connector)
#   - BOOST_SOL/GPO 1 stub (Superseal 2-way — repurposed for reverse light relay)
#   - Fuel pump relay trigger — GPO 2 (12-pin extra pin 3 / C)
#   - Fan relay trigger — GPO 6 (12-pin extra pin 4 / D)
#   - ECU +12V power — 12-pin extra pin 7 (G)
#   - Coil/INJ +12V — 12-pin extra pin 1 (A)
#   - Engine GND — 12-pin extra pin 2 (B) + cylinder head GND (brown wire)
#
# Items NOT in the M50 harness — must be wired separately (Phase 1):
#   [ ] EWS2 bypass (this file, Steps 1–2 above)
#   [ ] Alternator D+ excite — 12-pin pin 12 (M) + charge bulb (this file)
#   [ ] Starter trigger signal — 12-pin pin 6 (F) (this file)
#   [ ] Fuel pump hanger — harnesses/fuel-pump-hanger-phase1.wv
#   [ ] Flex fuel sensor — harnesses/flex-fuel-sensor-phase1.wv
#   [ ] 8HP CAN + power — harnesses/8hp-can.wv
#   [ ] 8HP reverse light relay — harnesses/8hp-body-integrations-phase1.wv
#   [ ] Gauge.S CAN cluster — harnesses/gauge-s-can.wv
#   [ ] DCT shifter paddle — harnesses/dct-shifter.wv
#   [ ] X20 body connector — harnesses/body-x20.wv
#   [ ] PST-F1 oil sensor — harnesses/pst-f1-sensor.wv
#   [ ] ATF temp sensor (optional) — harnesses/atf-temp-sensor.wv
#   [ ] EPS column-assist — harnesses/eps-column.wv
#   [ ] ID850 injector adapters — EV1-to-USCAR, ID PN 90.1, qty 6
#       (MaxxECU M50 harness uses EV1/JPT sockets; ID850 ships USCAR/EV6)
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

metadata:
  project: E36 Restomod — Phase 1 EWS2 Bypass + Starter/Alternator Supplemental
  description: >-
    EWS2 chassis bypass for MaxxECU M52 install.
    This is a chassis modification spec, not a harness build.
    See header comments for full procedure. Also documents the
    alternator D+ excite wire and starter trigger signal from the
    M50 pre-terminated harness 12-pin extra connector.

connectors:
  EWS2_MOD:
    type: EWS2 Module Connector (4-pin, gray, behind glovebox)
    pincount: 4
    pinlabels: [IGN_15, GND, STARTER_ENABLE, IMMO_KLINE]
    notes: >-
      MODIFICATION: short pins 1 and 3 (bridge IGN_15 to STARTER_ENABLE);
      remove or cut pin 4 (isolate IMMO_KLINE). The EWS2 module body can remain
      in place or be removed. Remove the ring antenna from the ignition lock ring
      if EWS2 module is physically removed.

  HARNESS_12PIN:
    type: MaxxECU M50 terminated harness — 12-pin extra connector (REV2)
    pincount: 12
    pinlabels:
      - "+12V_COIL_INJ"
      - ENGINE_GND
      - "GPO2_FUELPUMP"
      - "GPO6_FAN"
      - NC
      - STARTER_TRIGGER
      - "+12V_ECU"
      - NC
      - NC
      - NC
      - NC
      - "ALT_D_PLUS"
    notes: >-
      This connector is on the purchased M50 pre-terminated harness.
      Pins 1 (A), 2 (B), 3 (C), 4 (D), 7 (G) are connected to the
      power distribution relay board (Phase 1 discrete relay setup).
      Pin 6 (F): starter trigger signal to MaxxECU.
      Pin 12 (M): alternator D+ — connect via charge bulb to IGN+.

  CHARGE_BULB:
    type: Charge lamp — 3W–5W bayonet (W5W or equiv.)
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: [IGN_SIDE, ALT_SIDE]
    notes: >-
      Inline between +12V IGN (fused 5A) and 12-pin pin 12 (ALT_D_PLUS).
      Illuminates as battery warning when alternator is not charging;
      extinguishes once alternator output exceeds IGN supply voltage.
      Can route through OEM instrument cluster battery bulb holder if desired.

  IGN_SWITCH_START:
    type: Ignition switch — START position output
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["+12V_START"]
    notes: >-
      +12V present ONLY when key is held to START position (Kl.50).
      Connects to EWS2 pin 1 (and via bypass bridge to pin 3) and to
      HARNESS_12PIN pin 6 (STARTER_TRIGGER to MaxxECU).

cables:
  EWS_BYPASS_BRIDGE:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [RD]
    gauge: 18 AWG
    length: 0.1 m
    notes: Short jumper wire bridging EWS2 connector pins 1 and 3

  STARTER_SIGNAL:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [RDBK]
    gauge: 18 AWG
    length: 2.0 m
    notes: >-
      Ignition switch START output to MaxxECU 12-pin extra pin 6 (F).
      Routed from cabin ignition lock area through firewall grommet to engine bay.

  ALT_EXCITE:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [YEBK]
    gauge: 18 AWG
    length: 0.5 m
    notes: >-
      Alternator D+ excite: from charge bulb ALT_SIDE to 12-pin pin 12 (M).
      Engine-bay-side only; charge bulb and IGN source wire are cabin-side.

connections:
  -
    - IGN_SWITCH_START: ["+12V_START"]
    - EWS_BYPASS_BRIDGE: [1]
    - EWS2_MOD: [IGN_15]
  -
    - EWS2_MOD: [STARTER_ENABLE]
    - EWS_BYPASS_BRIDGE: [1]
    # Note: EWS_BYPASS_BRIDGE wire connects pin 1 to pin 3 (direct jumper)
  -
    - IGN_SWITCH_START: ["+12V_START"]
    - STARTER_SIGNAL: [1]
    - HARNESS_12PIN: [STARTER_TRIGGER]
  -
    - CHARGE_BULB: [ALT_SIDE]
    - ALT_EXCITE: [1]
    - HARNESS_12PIN: ["ALT_D_PLUS"]
